{
  "id": "COMPOUND:26277 - PROTEIN:5782",
  "verbalization": "Stecholide I is shown to interact with CMP-N-acetylneuraminate-beta-1,4-galactoside alpha-2,3-sialyltransferase, a protein that is a target of multiple compounds, including Leosibirone B and another compound with the structure (3aR,6S,6aR)-3,6-bis(3,4,5-trimethoxyphenyl)-1,3,3a,4,6,6a-hexahydrofuro[3,4-c]furan. All these targets are ultimately linked to DMS-273, a cell line that is likely involved in the biological process being targeted. The evidence suggests that Stecholide I may inhibit the activity of this enzyme, which could lead to a disruption in sialylation processes, potentially affecting cellular function and contributing to the observed effect on DMS-273. The integration of multiple pathways supports a mechanistic link between Stecholide I and DMS-273, though the exact mode of action remains to be fully elucidated. The presence of multiple targets and their shared downstream effect on DMS-273 indicates a potential for Stecholide I to exert its biological influence through a common pathway, which could be relevant for therapeutic applications.",
